{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":3,"lang":"es","title":"Cosas: a, an, the, this, these","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Qué vas a aprender a decir","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"En esta lección aprendes a nombrar las cosas que te rodean: «es una silla», «son entradas», «este cargador», «esas flores están frescas», «el error está aquí», «es una taza roja». Para eso el inglés usa palabritas delante: a, an, the, this, that."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a chair.","translation":"Es una silla.","hi":"a"},{"en":"They are tickets.","translation":"Son entradas.","hi":"tickets"},{"en":"This is a charger.","translation":"Esto es un cargador. *(en mi mano)*","hi":"This"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Esas flores están frescas.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"Es una taza roja.","hi":"red"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"Una cosa: a delante","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"a es como «un» o «una», pero no cambia: sirve igual para silla, lámpara o llave. Y en inglés hace falta It al principio: «Es una silla» es It is a chair, no Is a chair."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"It is","accent":true},{"text":"a","accent":true},{"text":"cosa","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a chair.","translation":"Es una silla.","hi":"a"},{"en":"It's a lamp.","translation":"Es una lámpara.","hi":"a"},{"en":"Is it a table?","translation":"¿Es una mesa?","hi":"a"},{"en":"It is a key.","translation":"Es una llave.","hi":"a"},{"en":"It is not a window.","translation":"No es una ventana.","hi":"a"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Is a chair.","right":"It is a chair."},{"wrong":"It is chair.","right":"It is a chair."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"a no tiene masculino ni femenino: a chair, a table, a key."}]},{"num":"03","title":"a o an: lo decide el primer sonido","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Si la palabra empieza con sonido de vocal, en vez de a se dice an: an armchair, an oven, an umbrella. Así se pronuncia más fácil, sin tropezar entre dos vocales."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an armchair.","translation":"Es un sillón.","hi":"an"},{"en":"Is it an oven?","translation":"¿Es un horno?","hi":"an"},{"en":"It's an umbrella.","translation":"Es un paraguas.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It is an earring.","translation":"Es un arete.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It's an egg.","translation":"Es un huevo.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It is an invoice.","translation":"Es una factura.","hi":"an"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a oven.","right":"It is an oven."},{"wrong":"It's a egg.","right":"It's an egg."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"It's","after":"umbrella.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":"an","why":"umbrella empieza con sonido de vocal, así que an."}}]},{"num":"04","title":"El sonido, no la letra","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Fíjate en el sonido, no en la letra. En hour la h no suena: se dice «auer», así que an hour. En cambio uniform y euro empiezan con sonido de «y» («yuniform», «yuro»): eso no es vocal, así que a."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an hour.","translation":"Es una hora.","hi":"an"},{"en":"Is it a uniform?","translation":"¿Es un uniforme?","hi":"a"},{"en":"It's a euro.","translation":"Es un euro.","hi":"a"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a hour.","right":"It is an hour."},{"wrong":"It's an euro.","right":"It's a euro."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Truco: di la palabra en voz alta. Si empieza con a, e, i, o, u — an. Si empieza con «y» o con consonante — a."}]},{"num":"05","title":"Varias cosas: añade s y quita a","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Para varias cosas se añade s: ticket → tickets. Y a desaparece, porque a significa «una». No hay «unos» delante: They are tickets, no They are a tickets. Y la pieza cambia: it is para una, they are para varias."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"They are","accent":true},{"text":"cosa + s","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are tickets.","translation":"Son entradas.","hi":"tickets"},{"en":"Are they coins?","translation":"¿Son monedas?","hi":"coins"},{"en":"The cards are new.","translation":"Las tarjetas son nuevas.","hi":"cards"},{"en":"They are towels.","translation":"Son toallas.","hi":"towels"},{"en":"They are spoons.","translation":"Son cucharas.","hi":"spoons"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are a tickets.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"Are tickets.","right":"They are tickets."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"El mensajero te da varias entradas. Di: «Son entradas».","answer":["They","are","tickets"],"slotLabels":["quién","pieza","qué"],"distractors":["a","ticket"]}}]},{"num":"06","title":"Cuándo hace falta es","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Si la palabra termina en s, sh o ch, una s sola no se pronuncia. Se añade es, y aparece una sílaba más: bus → buses, dish → dishes, watch → watches. Se oye: «basis», «dishis»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are buses.","translation":"Son autobuses.","hi":"buses"},{"en":"Are they dishes?","translation":"¿Son platos?","hi":"dishes"},{"en":"The watches are old.","translation":"Los relojes son viejos.","hi":"watches"},{"en":"They are glasses.","translation":"Son vasos.","hi":"glasses"},{"en":"Are they brushes?","translation":"¿Son cepillos?","hi":"brushes"},{"en":"The benches are here.","translation":"Los bancos están aquí.","hi":"benches"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are buss.","right":"They are buses."},{"wrong":"The watchs are old.","right":"The watches are old."}]}]},{"num":"07","title":"Cuándo y cambia a ies","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Si la palabra termina en y y antes hay consonante, la y se cambia por ies: battery → batteries, city → cities. Suena casi igual, solo que al final se oye una «s» suave."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are batteries.","translation":"Son pilas.","hi":"batteries"},{"en":"Are they countries?","translation":"¿Son países?","hi":"countries"},{"en":"Where are the stories?","translation":"¿Dónde están los cuentos?","hi":"stories"},{"en":"They are cities.","translation":"Son ciudades.","hi":"cities"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are batterys.","right":"They are batteries."},{"wrong":"Where are the storys?","right":"Where are the stories?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"Are they","after":"?","options":["countrys","countries","countryes"],"answer":"countries","why":"Antes de la y hay una consonante (r), así que y cambia a ies."}}]},{"num":"08","title":"this y that: cerca o allí","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"this es «esto» o «este», para lo que tienes cerca, en la mano. that es «eso» o «aquello», para lo que está lejos y señalas con el dedo. El inglés no distingue «ese» y «aquel»: todo lo lejano es that."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"This is a charger.","translation":"Esto es un cargador. *(en mi mano)*","hi":"This"},{"en":"This is an adapter.","translation":"Esto es un adaptador.","hi":"This"},{"en":"That is a screen.","translation":"Eso es una pantalla. *(allí)*","hi":"That"},{"en":"Is this a remote?","translation":"¿Esto es un control remoto?","hi":"this"},{"en":"Is that a button?","translation":"¿Eso es un botón?","hi":"that"},{"en":"That is not a keyring.","translation":"Eso no es un llavero.","hi":"That"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"La pantalla está en la pared del fondo. ¿Qué dices?","optionA":"This is a screen.","optionB":"That is a screen.","correct":"B","explain":"La pantalla está lejos, así que that."}}]},{"num":"09","title":"these y those: cuando son varias","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Para varias cosas, this pasa a these y that pasa a those. Y la pieza es are. Cerca: these are. Lejos: those are."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"una cerca: this is","accent":false},{"text":"varias cerca: these are","accent":false},{"text":"una lejos: that is","accent":false},{"text":"varias lejos: those are","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"These are shoes.","translation":"Estos son zapatos.","hi":"These"},{"en":"Those are blankets.","translation":"Esas son mantas.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"Are these socks new?","translation":"¿Estos calcetines son nuevos?","hi":"these"},{"en":"Those sheets are big.","translation":"Esas sábanas son grandes.","hi":"Those"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"This are shoes.","right":"These are shoes."},{"wrong":"These is shoes.","right":"These are shoes."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"are shoes.","options":["This","These","Those"],"answer":"These","why":"Son varios zapatos y están cerca: these."}}]},{"num":"10","title":"«Este álbum», «esas flores»","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"this, that, these, those pueden ir justo delante de la cosa: this album, those flowers. Entonces no hace falta a. A diferencia del español, la palabra no tiene género: this sirve para «este» y «esta»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"This album is big.","translation":"Este álbum es grande.","hi":"This"},{"en":"These frames are cheap.","translation":"Estos marcos son baratos.","hi":"These"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Esas flores están frescas.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"This building is new.","translation":"Este edificio es nuevo.","hi":"This"},{"en":"Is this lemon ripe?","translation":"¿Este limón está maduro?","hi":"this"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"This a album is big.","right":"This album is big."},{"wrong":"These frame are cheap.","right":"These frames are cheap."}]}]},{"num":"11","title":"a o the","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Igual que en español: a es «un/una», para algo que nombras por primera vez: A cashier is here. the es «el/la/los/las», cuando los dos ya saben de qué cosa se habla. The mistake is here. Pero the no cambia: sirve para todo."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"A cashier is here.","translation":"Hay un cajero aquí.","hi":"A"},{"en":"This is a receipt.","translation":"Esto es un recibo.","hi":"a"},{"en":"The mistake is here.","translation":"El error está aquí.","hi":"The"},{"en":"The handle is broken.","translation":"La manija está rota.","hi":"The"},{"en":"The seller is busy.","translation":"El vendedor está ocupado.","hi":"The"},{"en":"An item is missing.","translation":"Falta un artículo.","hi":"An"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"mistake is here.","options":["A","An","The"],"answer":"The","why":"Los dos saben de qué error se trata: the."}}]},{"num":"12","title":"Cosas en general: sin the","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Aquí el español engaña. Decimos «Los libros pesan» hablando de los libros en general. En inglés, para hablar de algo en general, no se pone the: Books are heavy. The books es solo para unos libros concretos."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Books are heavy.","translation":"Los libros pesan. *(en general)*","hi":"Books"},{"en":"Newspapers are cheap.","translation":"Los periódicos son baratos. *(en general)*","hi":"Newspapers"},{"en":"Wrenches are expensive.","translation":"Las llaves inglesas son caras. *(en general)*","hi":"Wrenches"},{"en":"The magazines are new.","translation":"Las revistas son nuevas. *(estas)*","hi":"The"},{"en":"The stairs are narrow.","translation":"La escalera es estrecha. *(de este edificio)*","hi":"The"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Hablas de los periódicos en general. ¿Qué dices?","optionA":"The newspapers are cheap.","optionB":"Newspapers are cheap.","correct":"B","explain":"En general, sin the: Newspapers are cheap."}}]},{"num":"13","title":"El color va delante y no cambia","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"En español decimos «una taza roja». En inglés es al revés: el color va delante — a red cup. Y el color nunca lleva s: black chairs, no blacks chairs. a o an depende del sonido de la palabra que va justo después: an olive coat."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"a / an / this / these","accent":true},{"text":"color o rasgo","accent":true},{"text":"cosa","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"Es una taza roja.","hi":"red"},{"en":"It is an olive coat.","translation":"Es un abrigo verde oliva.","hi":"an"},{"en":"These are black chairs.","translation":"Son sillas negras.","hi":"black"},{"en":"This round table is heavy.","translation":"Esta mesa redonda pesa.","hi":"round"},{"en":"These metal boxes are heavy.","translation":"Estas cajas de metal pesan.","hi":"metal"},{"en":"This striped scarf is new.","translation":"Esta bufanda de rayas es nueva.","hi":"striped"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a cup red.","right":"It is a red cup."},{"wrong":"These are blacks chairs.","right":"These are black chairs."},{"wrong":"It is a olive coat.","right":"It is an olive coat."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"El vendedor te pregunta qué taza quieres. Di: «Es una taza roja».","answer":["It","is","a","red","cup"],"slotLabels":["quién","pieza","una","cómo","qué"],"distractors":["an","reds"]}}]},{"num":"14","title":"Los errores que comete casi todo el mundo","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Is a chair.","right":"It is a chair."},{"wrong":"It is a oven.","right":"It is an oven."},{"wrong":"They are a tickets.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"This are shoes.","right":"These are shoes."},{"wrong":"It is a cup red.","right":"It is a red cup."},{"wrong":"These are blacks chairs.","right":"These are black chairs."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Antes de la cosa, pregúntate dos cosas. ¿Una o varias? Una: a/an, this/that. Varias: s al final, these/those, are. Y: ¿la otra persona sabe de cuál hablas? Si sí, the. Si hablas en general, nada."}]},{"num":"15","title":"Qué llevarte a la práctica","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Una cosa: a o an según el primer sonido. Varias: s y sin a. Cerca: this / these; lejos: that / those. Lo que los dos conocen: the. En general: sin the. El color, delante y sin s: a red cup."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an hour.","translation":"Es una hora.","hi":"an"},{"en":"They are batteries.","translation":"Son pilas.","hi":"batteries"},{"en":"Books are heavy.","translation":"Los libros pesan.","hi":"Books"},{"en":"The mistake is here.","translation":"El error está aquí.","hi":"The"},{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"Es una taza roja.","hi":"red"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{"1":"02","2":"02","3":"02","4":"02","5":"02","6":"02","7":"02","8":"02","9":"03","10":"03","11":"04","12":"04","13":"04","14":"04","15":"04","16":"04","17":"05","18":"05","19":"07","20":"07","21":"07","22":"07","23":"07","24":"07","25":"08","26":"08","27":"08","28":"08","29":"08","30":"08","31":"08","32":"08","33":"09","34":"09","35":"10","36":"10","37":"10","38":"10","39":"10","40":"10","41":"11","42":"11","43":"12","44":"12","45":"12","46":"12","47":"12","48":"12","49":"13","50":"13","51":"13","52":"13","53":"13","54":"13","55":"13","56":"13"}}
